.TH AGENDA 1 "September 2026" "Agenda 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agenda \- retain accountable work and project finite obligations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agenda apply
ROOT < change.json
.br
.B agenda export
ROOT
.br
.B agenda expand --as-of
TIME < schedule.json
.br
.B agenda project
SNAPSHOT
.B --as-of
TIME < observations.jsonl
.br
.B agenda version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Agenda records promises, schedule revisions, human reports and business
decisions. It does not execute work, approve actions, schedule jobs or notify
anybody. Only apply writes an explicitly selected physical absolute local root.
Export emits the complete self-contained account. Expand and project are pure
finite operations requiring explicit RFC3339 evaluation time.
.SH DATA
Apply reads one agenda.change/v1 object with request_id, kind, id, previous,
by, reason, value and optional selected evidence. Kinds are item, schedule,
report and disposition. Expected revisions serialize changes; repeating the
same request ID and bytes returns the original commitment. Evidence files are
retained and verified by SHA-256. Extensions remain opaque data.
.PP
Project reads a complete agenda.snapshot/v1 file and an observation JSONL
stream on stdin. It prints one agenda.projection/v1 object. Missing, stale and
unknown evidence remains visible. Caller observations are not authenticated
acceptance. Human completion is reported-done, distinct from accepted work.
.PP
Expand reads one finite schedule and emits all occurrence records as JSONL.
Weekdays use Monday=0. Local times require an IANA timezone; ambiguous or
nonexistent times fail. Catch-up policy changes eligibility, never accountability.
.SH FILES
ROOT/snapshot.json is an atomically replaced complete hash-chained logical
history with retained evidence. ROOT/.lock serializes local writers. Export and
pure commands neither lock nor write. No network-filesystem or distributed
transaction guarantee is made.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means successful operation, even when work is overdue or incomplete.
1 means rejected, conflicting or inconsistent input.
2 means usage or operating failure. Diagnostics go to stderr.
A failed apply reply may follow commitment: repeat the identical request ID.
.SH LIMITS
Inputs use strict bounded UTF-8 JSON. Account limits are 2000 records, 64 MiB
retained evidence and a 128 MiB snapshot. Schedule ranges cover at most 366
dates. No pruning or history deletion is provided.
.SH SEE ALSO
README.md and DESIGN.md describe the complete schemas and trust boundaries.
